Commands used in the video in step by step order:

Update the system: 
sudo apt update

Use sudo apt upgrade if you have many packages that need an upgrade

Install the helper tools: 
sudo apt install wget gpg apt-transport-https -y

Download Microsoft's key: 
wget -qO- https://packages.microsoft.com/keys/microsoft.asc | gpg --dearmor > packages.microsoft.gpg

Move the key into place:   
sudo install -o root -g root -m 644 packages.microsoft.gpg /usr/share/keyrings/

Add the VS Code source:
echo "deb [arch=amd64 signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/packages.microsoft.gpg] https://packages.microsoft.com/repos/code stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/vscode.list

Install VS Code: 
sudo apt update
sudo apt install code -y

Launch it:
code
